From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Janowski <janaz9@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: do not force SGMII mode on QCA8337

Since 6.12.109 (stable backport), qca8k_pcs_config() sets
QCA8K_PORT_PAD_SGMII_FORCE_MODE on QCA8337 whenever phylink uses
out-of-band negotiation, which is the case for a fixed-link CPU port.

IPQ50xx boards such as the GL.iNet GL-B3000 connect the QCA8337 CPU port
to the SoC MAC over SGMII with a fixed-link, and the SoC side still
auto-negotiates (see "net: dsa: qca8k: always enable SGMII
auto-negotiation"). Forcing the switch side breaks the CPU link, so no
traffic passes between the LAN ports and the SoC.

Keep the force bit cleared.

Signed-off-by: Tomasz Janowski <janaz9@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1616,14 +1616,13 @@ static int qca8k_pcs_config(struct phyli
 			QCA8K_PORT0_PAD_SGMII_TXCLK_FALLING_EDGE) : 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * (Un)set force mode on QCA8337 only, don't include it in the mask for
-	 * others. It is written to the PORT0 PAD register for both port 0 and 6.
+	 * Always clear force mode on QCA8337 only, don't include it in the mask
+	 * for others. The SoC side of the CPU link keeps auto-negotiating, see
+	 * "net: dsa: qca8k: always enable SGMII auto-negotiation". It is written
+	 * to the PORT0 PAD register for both port 0 and 6.
 	 */
-	if (priv->switch_id == QCA8K_ID_QCA8337) {
-		if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_OUTBAND)
-			val |= QCA8K_PORT_PAD_SGMII_FORCE_MODE;
+	if (priv->switch_id == QCA8K_ID_QCA8337)
 		mask |= QCA8K_PORT_PAD_SGMII_FORCE_MODE;
-	}
 
 	if (mask)
 		ret = qca8k_rmw(priv, reg, mask, val);
